{
  "manufacturer": "Mitsubishi Electric",
  "manufacturer_slug": "mitsubishi-electric",
  "model": "FR-A700 inverter (RS-485 terminals, Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "fr-a700",
  "short_model": "FR-A700",
  "aliases": [
    "FR-A720",
    "FR-A740",
    "FR-A700 series"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "FR-A700 series inverters (FR-A720-0.4K to 90K, FR-A740-0.4K to 500K) using the RS-485 terminals with Pr.549 = 1 (Modbus-RTU); Instruction Manual (Applied) revision E.",
  "summary": "Mitsubishi Electric's previous-generation high-performance inverter. Its RS-485 terminal block can speak Modbus RTU, exposing system variables (control word, operation mode, frequency command) at 40002-40015, a real-time monitor block from 40201, fault history at 40501 and parameters 0-999 at 41000 + parameter number. This map covers control, status, monitors, fault codes and the communication parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The manual prints Modicon-style register numbers (40002, 41004) and states: starting address = register number - 40001. Its example reads 41004 (Pr.4) with start address H03EB (1003)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "FR-A700 Instruction Manual (Applied)",
    "doc_number": "IB(NA)-0600226ENG-E",
    "revision_date": "2012-02",
    "url": "https://dl.mitsubishielectric.com/dl/fa/document/manual/inv/ib0600226eng/ib0600226enge.pdf",
    "pages": "Printed pp. 347-358 (4.24.6 Modbus-RTU communication specifications, example p. 350, Modbus registers pp. 355-358 incl. fault code list p. 358); parameter list pp. 71 ff."
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are single 16-bit words.",
    "Left out because the increment depends on capacity (55K or lower / 75K or higher): output current 40202, current peak 40211, input power 40213, output power 40214, excitation current 40218 and motor output 40234. Motor load factor 40224 gives a size-independent current reading.",
    "Left out because the sign is not stated: motor torque 40207, torque command 40232, torque current command 40233 and PID deviation 40254. Vector-control position/orientation monitors (40219, 40222, 40235), option terminal monitors (40258-40260) and the version-dependent motor temperature 40246 are not listed.",
    "Frequency registers use 0.01 Hz; with Pr.37/Pr.144 speed display they switch to 1 unit. The 0.01 Hz unit for 40014/40015 comes from the same manual's computer-link set-frequency description.",
    "Fault history registers hold the fault code in the low byte; the values listed are the manual's fault code list.",
    "Parameters with a 9999 (function off) setting are listed with their normal increment; the manual does not say how the 9999 setting itself is encoded on the wire.",
    "Parameters 0-999 sit at 41000 + Pr. number; calibration parameters C2-C41 have their own registers and are not listed. Pr.7/Pr.8 are left out (increment depends on Pr.21)."
  ],
